        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-09-20T09:50:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The other folks answered 2 &amp; 3, but I had an additional thought on 1: I always assumed these cards meant \"Active Player\", as an incapacitated player doesn't have cards. Given that assumption, it resolves the confusion. That's just me, though!</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li>Yes Police Backup would be destroyed instead of the hero discarding a card. If multiple heroes have to discard a card only one player&nbsp;wouldn't have to.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Have to disagree on this - the discard is just a trigger for the Police Backup effect, as Police Backup doesn't say \"instead\".</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ketigid\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/9fc29f/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ketigid:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>Yes, if Infected heroes can remain infected and deal damage, so can they skip their turns.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Infected? &lt;Insert \"Confused\" emoticon here&gt;</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:12:34.919Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
